<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name      "ugreen-led-control">
<!ENTITY author    "Alexander Schubert">
<!ENTITY version   "0.19.0">
<!ENTITY launch    "Settings/UGREENLEDControl">
<!ENTITY repo      "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alexanderschubert/ugreen-led-control">
<!ENTITY gitURL    "&repo;/v&version;">
<!ENTITY releaseURL "https://github.com/alexanderschubert/ugreen-led-control/releases/download/v&version;">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "&repo;/main/plugin/ugreen-led-control.plg">
<!ENTITY bootDIR   "/boot/config/plugins/&name;">
<!ENTITY srcDIR    "&bootDIR;/&version;">
]>

<PLUGIN
  name="&name;"
  author="&author;"
  version="&version;"
  launch="&launch;"
  pluginURL="&pluginURL;"
  icon="ugreen-led-control.png"
  min="7.0.0"
  support="https://forums.unraid.net/topic/200791-plugin-ugreen-led-control-led-control-for-ugreen-dxdxp-nas/"
>

<CHANGES>

### 0.19.0
- Light colour scheme: Settings → System → Appearance offers Dark, Light or "Same as Unraid" (follows your Unraid theme); the dashboard tile follows it too

### 0.18.0
- Every setting saves on change: status display, night mode and Unraid alerts no longer need a Save button
- Night mode: the brightness slider and the on/off switch show the day settings instead of the dimmed LEDs, with a note until when night mode runs; a brightness changed at night is saved for the day and the LEDs stay dimmed
- Ready for a Spanish translation (shown once it exists); Unraid's Spanish locale is detected

### 0.17.3
- Fix: a colour typed as a hex value now shows in its preview swatch right away (reported in the forum)

### 0.17.2
- Every download is checked against its MD5, so the plugin manager only installs the files of this version (Community Applications review)
- The ugreen-led-i2c binary is built reproducibly; nothing changes in how it works

### 0.17.1
- Fix: LEDs could be missing after a reboot with "no SMBus I801 adapter found" (DXP8800 Plus, GitHub issue #30); the plugin now loads the Intel SMBus driver itself and waits for the adapter
- New `ugreen-led-ctl smbus` shows the adapter or the kernel messages why it is missing

### 0.17.0
- Disks in standby can pulse slowly in their colour (Drives → Status display → Disks in standby → Pulse slowly)
- The network LED setting moved to the overview, right below the default mode, and saves on change

### 0.16.0
- Status display: the network LED can blink with traffic (as before), only show the link without blinking, or stay manual while the bay LEDs keep showing disk activity (GitHub issue #27)
- A manual network LED keeps its own colour, brightness and effect, also rainbow/temperature, in status mode

### 0.15.2
- The Support link on the Plugins page opens the support thread in the Unraid forum

### 0.15.1
- Fix: "Standby" broke over two lines in the small case pictures; the text in the bays now scales with the bay width
- Fix: long effect names ("Temperature") were cut off in narrow effect tiles

### 0.15.0
- Dashboard tile: Unraid's dashboard (6.12+) gets a "UGREEN LED Control" tile with the case picture, live LED colours, each bay's temperature or state, and mode / night / alert
- Own icon (the NAS front with coloured LEDs) on the Plugins page, the settings page, the dashboard tile and in the plugin's sidebar

### 0.14.2
- Fix: the LED tables showed the controller's internal LED name ("disk1") under each bay, which looked like the Unraid slot; they now show the Unraid disk in the bay (e.g. "disk2 · /dev/sdc")

### 0.14.1
- The case pictures on the overview show each bay's temperature or state (standby, error, SMART) in the middle of the bay

### 0.14.0
- More UGREEN models: DXP8800 Plus, DX4600 Pro, DXP4800 (Plus/Pro), DX4700 and DXP2800 get their bay-to-SATA-port tables (after miskcoo/ugreen_leds_controller); other models fall back to ata1…ataN
- The System page says whether the bay assignment is verified, reported or guessed; the Laufwerke page asks to check it with "Identifizieren" when it isn't verified

### 0.13.0
- Drive LEDs can show each disk's temperature (blue → green → yellow at Unraid's "hot" → red at "critical"; disk-specific limits and SSD limits respected)
- SMART warnings: a bay lights up in a warning colour when reallocated, pending or uncorrectable sectors grow, a SMART value fails, or Unraid counts read/write errors; "Quittieren" accepts the current values
- Fix: short status badges on the bay cards no longer turn into circles

### 0.12.0
- Status mode shows parity checks and rebuilds: array disks breathe in their own colour (disks with errors keep the error colour); the Laufwerke page shows the progress
- Spun-down disks are dimmed (or normal / off, as chosen); bay cards show standby, temperature and read/write errors

### 0.11.0
- Unraid alerts: while Unraid has unread warnings (or only alerts, as chosen), the power LED blinks in the alert colour; once they are read or archived it returns to normal (System page, checked every minute)

### 0.10.0
- Identify a bay: "Identifizieren" on the Laufwerke page blinks the bay's LED white for 30 seconds, then restores its previous state; the status daemon leaves it alone meanwhile

### 0.9.0
- The interface speaks German and English: System → Sprache / Language, with "Automatic" following Unraid's language

### 0.8.0
- Rainbow effect: a colour wave over the chosen LEDs, with speed and direction
- Temperature effect: the LEDs show the CPU temperature from blue (35 °C) over green and yellow to red (65 °C)
- "Nur im Leerlauf" pauses both while a disk is busy
- Picking a colour or another effect for an LED ends a rainbow/temperature effect on it; in status mode they apply to the power LED only

### 0.7.0
- Night mode (Zeitpläne): from a start to an end time, also across midnight, the LEDs are dimmed to a night brightness or switched off; in status mode disk and network LEDs follow, and dark LEDs don't blink

### 0.6.1
- Status mode is easier to recognise: disk and network LEDs show "Statusmodus" instead of a greyed-out effect field, and the LED and Laufwerke pages explain what the mode does

### 0.6.0
- No kernel module any more: the plugin talks to the LED controller itself (ugreen-led-i2c over /dev/i2c-N), so Unraid updates with a new kernel keep the LEDs working
- Status mode blinks disks and the network LED with the controller's own blink while there is activity
- A led_ugreen driver from an older version is unloaded; its cached copy on the boot device is removed

### 0.5.1
- Fix: without ugreenleds-driver no LEDs appeared, because the LED controller was never declared on the SMBus; the plugin now does that itself
- The System page shows whether the LED controller is really declared and which LEDs were found, instead of fixed values

### 0.5.0
- Status mode: disk LEDs blink on activity and switch to the error colour when Unraid reports a disabled, invalid or missing disk; empty bays stay dark; the network LED blinks with traffic and turns to the error colour without link or gateway
- Bays are matched to disks by SATA port (DXP6800 Pro), shown on the Laufwerke page
- The status daemon steps aside while the ugreenleds-driver monitor is running

### 0.4.0
- Settings made in the web interface are saved on the boot device (USB flash drive or SSD) and restored at boot

### 0.3.0
- New interface: overview with general settings, LED colours, effects, live preview of the case and effect settings
- Per-LED page and per-bay page with colour, brightness and effect
- Test button and reset to defaults
- Warning while the ugreenleds-driver LED monitor is running, because it overwrites disk and network LEDs
- Styles only apply inside the plugin page

### 0.2.1
- Fix: the install script copied nothing, because plugin entities are not expanded inside CDATA

### 0.2.0
- Plugin downloads its files from GitHub instead of expecting them on the flash drive
- LED writes from the settings page work (they go through api.php with the WebGUI csrf_token)
- Only the bays the model really has are shown (DXP6800 Pro: 6)
- Reading an LED returns valid JSON again
- An led_ugreen driver loaded by another plugin is left alone
- Success and error messages are visible
- The page lives at Settings → User Utilities → UGREEN LED Control

### 0.1.0
- Initial release

</CHANGES>

